# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public-release boundary
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The framework repository is code-only. The journal manuscript, AIHealth
# conference camera-ready, aggregate result tables, internal planning notes,
# and reviewer-feedback drafts all live under these paths locally but are not
# redistributed publicly. They are kept on disk so authors can keep working
# without re-creating them, but git will not track them.

submissions/
download.zip
download.zip.txt

# Manuscript sources and the aggregate tables they are verified against ARE
# part of the release -- the Data availability statement names them, and
# scripts/verify_paper_numbers.py needs both to run in a fresh clone. What
# stays local is the internal planning record (Turkish decision register,
# framework anatomy), superseded working drafts, and the raster duplicates of
# figures that ship as vector PDFs.
# Springer Nature ships sn-jnl.cls and its .bst files under its own terms, so
# they are fetched rather than redistributed here (see README, "Building the
# manuscript"). The paper/* rule below already excludes them.
paper/*
!paper/tables/
paper/tables/*
!paper/splitguard_ad.tex
!paper/splitguard_ad.pdf
!paper/SplitGuard-AD_Supplementary_Material.tex
!paper/SplitGuard-AD_Supplementary_Material.pdf
!paper/SplitGuard-AD_GraphicalAbstract.pdf
!paper/references.bib
!paper/fig01_leakage_taxonomy.pdf
!paper/fig04a_seed_stability.pdf
!paper/fig04b_metric_comparison.pdf
!paper/fig05_learning_curves.pdf
!paper/fig06_cross_cohort_inflation.pdf
!paper/fig07_arm_forest.pdf
!paper/fig08_degradation_curve.pdf
!paper/fig09_cost_of_leakage.pdf
!paper/fig10_operating_point.pdf
!paper/fig11_dose_response.pdf
!paper/fig12_provenance_degradation.pdf
!paper/figS1_subgroup_auroc.pdf
!paper/tables/adni_demographics.tex
!paper/tables/adni_inflation_gap.tex
!paper/tables/gpu_numbers.tex
!paper/tables/tier1_truth.tex
!paper/tables/oasis_replication.tex
!paper/tables/adni_robustness.tex
!paper/tables/adni_subject_level.tex
!paper/tables/operating_point.tex

# Aggregate ADNI result tables are released; the download inventory is not --
# its relative_path column carries DUA-protected ADNI study-file and
# participant paths.
reports/*
!reports/rerun_comparison.md
!reports/tables/
reports/tables/*
!reports/tables/adni/
reports/tables/adni/adni_inventory.csv

# Cross-cohort aggregate tables that verify_paper_numbers.py reads from the
# tables root. Without these the verifier silently skips the Tier-1 and
# OASIS-1 replication claims and the two probe results, and still reports a
# clean pass -- so a reader would see 103 checks succeed and never learn that
# 22 were never attempted.
!reports/tables/jpeg_inflation_gap_bootstrap.json
!reports/tables/oasis1_inflation_gap_bootstrap.json
# Tier-1 provenance recovered against OASIS-1: aggregate counts and
# calibration only, no image-to-participant mapping.
!reports/tables/tier1_ground_truth_audit.json
!reports/tables/tier1_split_rules_vs_truth.json
# The cross-cohort hierarchical intervals, for the same reason as above: the
# manuscript quotes all three, the bootstrap tree they are computed in is not
# released, and without these a reader checking the paper against this
# repository is told four artefacts are absent rather than that the claims
# hold. Seed-level aggregates, no identifiers.
!reports/tables/tier1_hierarchical.json
!reports/tables/oasis1_hierarchical.json
!reports/tables/oasis1_densenet121_hierarchical.json
# Cited by name in the manuscript (\S subject-level aggregation), so it has
# to ship or the citation is false. Pure aggregate counts from a public
# cohort: no identifiers, no paths, no clinical fields per participant.
!reports/tables/oasis1_subject_level_summary.json

# Keep two canonical methodology docs in the public release; exclude
